  "instruction": "Using Visual Studio Code, create a Python script named `credit_decision_rule.py` in the `/home/user/analysis_results/` directory. The dataset `credit_approval.csv` is already located in the same directory. In this script, load the dataset using pandas. Build a simple rule-based classifier that flags applicants as 'risky' when (A2 < 25 and A14 > 1000) or (A8 < 2). Encode the target column 'A16' so that '+' becomes 1 (approved) and '−' becomes 0 (risky). Compute the precision and recall of this decision rule compared to the true target class, treating the predicted 'risky' applicants as class 0. Save the results to a text file named `credit_decision_rule_metrics.txt` with two lines in the format: 'Precision: <value>' and 'Recall: <value>'. Round both metrics to four decimal places.",
